  "Close about the atlas": "关闭关于图谱",
  "A NOTE FROM THE ATLAS": "关于这幅图谱",
  "Knowledge is a conversation": "知识是一场",
  "across centuries.": "跨越世纪的对话。",
  "The Tower of Science maps how ideas build on, challenge, and transform one another. It is a curated guide to scientific development, not a complete family tree of human knowledge.": "科学之塔展示思想如何相互奠基、质疑与转化。它是一份经过编选的科学发展指南，并非人类知识的完整谱系。",
  "Ideas": "概念",
  "Journeys": "导览",
  "Reading the tower": "如何阅读科学之塔",
  "Earlier milestones sit lower; later ones sit higher. Approximate contemporaries share period floors, with exact dates preserved in the index. Cards are centered within their subbranch cells. Science sections reserve separate horizontal regions within each era and expand to accommodate their busiest floor. The shape stays fixed when filtering. At far zoom, inactive branches become named summaries within their eras. Labels retain a readable size and may shift to avoid collisions; the underlying concept positions do not move. Selecting a branch name reveals its concepts while keeping your current selection and filters. Summary connections group the same cited relationships and do not create new historical claims. Time is compressed, and spacing is not a measure of importance or difficulty. Multiple roots acknowledge that counting, observation, craft, and practical knowledge arose in many communities. Unrecorded contributions cannot be reconstructed with certainty.": "较早的里程碑位于下方，较晚的位于上方。大致同时代的概念共用时间层，精确日期保留在索引中。卡片在所属分支的格位内居中排列。每个时代为各学科划分独立的水平区域，并按最拥挤的时间层预留空间。筛选不会改变布局。缩小视图时，非活跃分支会在原位置合并为带名称的概览；标签保持可读，概念本身的位置不变。选择分支名称可展开其中的概念，同时保留当前选择与筛选。概览连线汇总原有的、有来源的联系，不新增历史主张。时间经过压缩，间距不代表重要性或难度。多个起点体现计数、观察、工艺和实践知识曾在不同群体中产生；没有留下记录的贡献无法被确切重建。",
  "Four kinds of connection": "四种联系",
  "Documented connections are supported by the cited accounts. Conceptual connections are editorial interpretations of prerequisites, not evidence of historical transmission. Contested links identify uncertainty. The graph represents development without claiming that history was inevitable.": "有文献依据的联系由所引材料支持。概念性联系是编者对前提依赖的解释，并非历史传承的证据。争议性联系明确标示不确定性。图谱呈现科学的发展，但不将其描述为必然进程。",
  "Sections, floors, and connection bundles": "学科分区、时间层与连接束",
  "Modern branches are navigational categories applied retrospectively, not claims about how historical communities divided knowledge. Each idea has one primary location; related branches identify interdisciplinary associations. Empty periods are omitted. Floors span prehistory, 500 years from 5000–500 BCE, 100 years to 1500, 25 years to 1850, 10 years to 1900, and five years afterward, split at era boundaries.": "现代学科分支是回溯性的导航分类，不代表历史上的人们也如此划分知识。每个概念有一个主要位置，相关分支用于标记跨学科关联。没有概念的时段予以省略。史前时期单独成层；公元前5000至前500年每层跨度500年，其后至1500年为100年，至1850年为25年，至1900年为10年，再后为5年。时间层在时代边界处分开。",
  "Bundled mode groups existing connections by section (or subbranch at closer zoom), era pair, relationship type, and evidence classification. Counts include distinct relationships after filters. Selected ideas show their immediate connections individually. Open a bundle to inspect its complete evidence or expand its members. Focus only hides background links; All connections draws each relationship. Bundles do not affect ancestry, pillar counts, or scientific standing.": "“合并为连接束”按学科分区（放大后按分支）、时代组合、联系类型和证据分类汇总已有联系。计数反映筛选后互不重复的联系。选中概念后，其直接联系单独显示。打开连接束可查看全部依据，也可展开其中的连线。“仅显示焦点”隐藏背景联系；“所有联系”逐条绘制关系。连接束不改变起源追溯、支柱计数或科学地位。",
  "What makes a pillar?": "何谓支柱？",
  "A pillar has five or more distinct, supported direct descendants in this edition. Documented and explicitly identified conceptual links count; contested links do not. Total descendants include indirect paths, counted once per concept. These are properties of this collection, not universal rankings of scientific value.": "本版中，一根支柱须有至少五个互不重复、有依据的直接后继概念。有文献依据和明确标注的概念性联系计入，争议性联系不计入。后继总数包括间接路径，每个概念只计算一次。这些指标描述本图谱的收录情况，并非科学价值的普遍排名。",
  "Dates, credit, and scientific standing": "日期、贡献归属与科学地位",
  "Dates usually identify a publication, formulation, observation, or surviving record. Approximate dates and disputed priority are explained inside entries. Credit includes named contributors and collective traditions. Superseded models remain visible for their historical role; useful approximations retain their domains of validity. Open questions and speculative proposals carry explicit labels.": "日期通常对应出版、理论表述、观测或现存记录。条目内会解释近似日期与优先权争议。贡献归属涵盖具名人物与集体传统。被取代的模型仍因其历史作用而保留；有用的近似模型会说明适用范围。未解问题与推测性提议均有明确标记。",
  "Sources and editorial approach": "来源与编写原则",
  "Entries cite scholarly histories, original research, textbooks, museums, and scientific institutions. Citations beside the introduction and history link claims to their supporting sources. Edge citations support the stated relationship or the ingredients of a conceptual inference. Guided tours are narratives through the atlas; consecutive stops do not imply a direct derivation.": "条目引用学术史著、原始研究、教材、博物馆和科学机构的资料。简介与历史叙述旁的引用把主张与支持材料相连。联系的引用支持所述关系，或概念性推断所依据的要素。主题导览是贯穿图谱的叙述，相邻站点不意味着存在直接推导关系。",
  "Coverage includes natural and formal sciences and selected social sciences. The collection is an introductory, source-linked synthesis, not a substitute for specialist historical review. Its sources and interpretations can be revised as evidence improves.": "收录范围包括自然科学、形式科学及部分社会科学。这是一份附有来源的入门综合介绍，不能替代专业的历史研究。随着证据改进，来源与解释都可以修订。",
